  "stories": [
    {
      "title": "CoreWeave reignites the AI trade.",
      "body": "CoreWeave jumped 24.7% Wednesday, its biggest gain in more than three months, after Q3 revenue of $3.66B (+168%) beat its own guide and it raised 2026 guidance to $13.0–13.3B. Chips led: semis +5.6%, Sandisk +14%, Micron and Dell +12%, AMD +7%. Apple closed at a record near $356 (about $5.2 trillion). Microsoft, Meta and Amazon fell about 2%, so the rally was narrow at the top."
    },
    {
      "title": "December hike is the base case.",
      "body": "Tuesday's October CPI rose 0.4% (0.3% expected) and core 0.3% (0.2% expected), a third straight 0.3% core print; no year-on-year figure was published because October 2025 data was never collected during the shutdown. Waller backs a December hike and floated 50bp; Logan wants two more. Prediction markets price a 25bp hike at about 85% and 50bp at about 10%. Next: jobless claims Thursday (195K expected), October PPI Friday (+0.4% m/m expected) and a heavy Fed speaker slate.",
